 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev. 10, 21 December 2021",
  "pages": 13
 },
 "summary": "Four independent bidirectional CMOS switches in one 14-lead SO package, each with two signal terminals (nY, nZ) and its own enable (nE). A switch conducts while its enable is HIGH and opens while it is LOW. It runs from a single 3 V to 15 V supply, with characteristics given at 5 V, 10 V and 15 V, over -40 °C to +125 °C. The control inputs carry clamp diodes, so a series current-limiting resistor lets them take voltages above VDD.",
