 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Each of the four switches is closed while its nE input is HIGH and open while it is LOW. The two terminals nY and nZ are interchangeable; signal passes in either direction."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Control inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The inputs have clamp diodes, so a voltage higher than VDD can drive them through a series resistor that limits the clamp current (rated ±10 mA). Edge rates must be no slower than 3.75 µs/V at VDD = 5 V, 0.5 µs/V at 10 V and 0.08 µs/V at 15 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Signal range and current direction",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Switch terminals stay between VSS and VDD. Switch current is rated ±10 mA. When current flows in at nY, more than 0.4 V across the switch lets VDD current flow out at nZ; current flowing in at nZ has no such limit."
  },
  {
   "topic": "ON resistance",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "At VDD = 5 V the ON resistance peaks sharply near mid-supply (about 350 Ω typ near 2.5 V input) and is near 115 Ω at either rail. At 10 V and 15 V it is much flatter, between roughly 40 Ω and 90 Ω across the signal range. Channels match within 25 Ω typ at 5 V, 10 Ω at 10 V and 5 Ω at 15 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Ratings and protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "ESD withstand exceeds 2000 V HBM (JESD22-A114F) and 200 V MM (JESD22-A115-B). The part meets JEDEC JESD 13-B and is fully static. Total dissipation is rated 500 mW, 100 mW per switch."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Analog and digital multiplexing and demultiplexing, and signal gating."
  }
 ],
